WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.182
The kit comes with six
fictional waiting records,

2
00:00:03.182 --> 00:00:06.162
one per outcome, and the
lab runs them on two days.

3
00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:09.874
The first is a reverted native
change, and it verifies.

4
00:00:09.874 --> 00:00:15.037
The second is a terminated user still
enabled in Entra ID: a mismatch.

5
00:00:15.037 --> 00:00:18.937
The third is an ISC account read
before it was re-aggregated.

6
00:00:18.937 --> 00:00:23.638
At noon on November first it's pending;
by noon the next day it's a mismatch.

7
00:00:23.638 --> 00:00:26.712
The fourth, an attribute change, verifies.

8
00:00:26.712 --> 00:00:30.144
The fifth is a native change
with an empty intended state,

9
00:00:30.144 --> 00:00:31.824
and it's skipped by the guard.

10
00:00:31.824 --> 00:00:35.537
The sixth, an orphan account
that was disabled, verifies.

11
00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:37.413
Why does the third one change?

12
00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:40.867
It started waiting at six in
the morning on November first,

13
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:45.257
so by noon on November second its
twenty-four-hour grace period has passed,

14
00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:47.830
and the stale read now
counts as a mismatch.
